Body:
I traced this against the V1 workflow and the current V2 plugin. V2 already made two intentional choices: #43710 allows writes under `~/.opencode/plan`, while #46905 keeps planning conversational by default and writes a document only when the user explicitly asks. I think the session-file workflow should preserve both decisions rather than restore V1 wholesale.

Proposed V2 scope:

- derive one stable path from the durable session creation timestamp + slug, under the existing global Plan directory;
- include that exact path in the Plan reminder, while retaining the explicit-user-request condition;
- enforce that session-specific file in the write/edit/patch hook instead of exposing the whole Plan directory to every Plan session;
- when switching from Plan to Build, mention the canonical path only if the file exists; keep the normal agent switch instead of reintroducing the V1 `plan_exit` tool.

I would cover stable derivation across reminder reconciliation/restart, exact-file permission boundaries, no eager file creation, and the conditional Build handoff. Would this V2-shaped scope be acceptable for implementation?
